Short:        MUI front-end for ZSetup
Author:       Denis Costils, with help from ChatGPT/Codex
Uploader:     Denis Costils
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      0.1
Requires:     MUI, ZSetup, OctoPrint
Architecture: m68k-amigaos

ZSetupMUI is a small MUI front-end for the ZSetup command line tool.

Place these two executables in your 3dtoolbox: assign:

  ZSetup
  ZSetupMUI

ZSetupMUI calls:

  3dtoolbox:ZSetup

No path configuration is needed, but the 3dtoolbox: assign must exist.

Use the Set button to store the current known Z offset, for example:

  0.00

Then press Start to home the printer, run auto-level, enable bed leveling
and move the nozzle to the center at Z 0.5.

Use:

  Z -0.05
  Z +0.05

to adjust by small 0.05 mm steps. Each step also sends M851 and M500 through
ZSetup, so the value is saved in the printer EEPROM.

When you quit ZSetupMUI, it calls:

  ZSetup HOME

so the printer returns to home with G28.

Keep a sheet of paper under the nozzle and keep your hand near the printer
stop/power button while testing.

For distribution, ZSetupMUI starts at 0.00 by default for safety. Do not use
this tool unless you understand the correct Z-offset direction for your printer.
A wrong Z-offset can make the nozzle hit the bed.

ZSetup refuses offsets outside this range:

  -5.00 mm to +5.00 mm
